# Streamlit is run by its own binary, not by python, and it takes the port and
# address as flags rather than from the environment. This one line is what
# makes it deployable anywhere:
#   --server.address 0.0.0.0  it binds loopback otherwise, which in a container
#                             means itself and nobody else
#   --server.port $PORT       it would sit on 8501 and ignore the platform
#   --server.headless         skips the first-run email prompt and the attempt
#                             to open a browser that isn't there
web: streamlit run app.py --server.port ${PORT:-8501} --server.address 0.0.0.0 --server.headless true --browser.gatherUsageStats false
